# BP QA–Development Cooperation Process

When working under `BP QA/`:

1. Do not inherit or reconstruct agreements from the previous BP QA Ways of Working.
2. Treat working-session decisions as **Draft**. Mark them **Agreed** only after review by the necessary stakeholders.
3. Mark proposals, assumptions, and loose ends clearly; do not silently turn them into policy.
4. Verify Trinity details from `Trinity/`. Verify Legion from https://docs-dts.appfire.net/platform-documentation/qa-coe/legion/ and this page. Do not invent extra Legion behaviour.
5. The target is one succinct Confluence page covering responsibilities, tools, epic acceptance testing, automation and maintenance, capacity, active initiatives, agreements, and unresolved decisions.
6. Follow [`BP QA/SKILL.md`](BP QA/SKILL.md).
